              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "जुहोति — juhoti — \"offers into the fire\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "वधूः अग्नौ लाजान् जुहोति। vadhūḥ agnau lājān juhoti. The bride offers puffed rice into the fire."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (he …): सः अग्नौ लाजान् हुतवान्, saḥ agnau lājān hutavān."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "जुहोति (juhoti) comes from the root √hu, \"to offer into the fire\", a third-class verb that doubles the root (ju-ho-ti); MW's ppp huta is \"offered in fire\" (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
